35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The fixed costs are 280,000 yen, but fuel is wildly uneven. Two people bought most of it. We need a fairer split.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the data confirms my fear. The other households soured because asking for favours felt like a debt. We need a system that removes the ""ask"" entirely.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, uneven fuel is a symptom. The real issue is the car’s state. I found it twice with the fuel light on and rubbish inside. That is unacceptable.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Minako, the receipts confirm the imbalance. Two people bought over half the fuel. @Asuka, the car’s state is irrelevant if the usage is skewed. We need to price the actual hours, not just the litres.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, the diary shows Saturday is triple Tuesday. @Asuka, the mechanic said short runs kill the brakes. That explains the extra arranging time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, pricing hours is logical, but the fixed 280,000 yen baseline is the real anchor. We must separate that from variable fuel costs to see who is actually subsidizing whom.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, separating costs is smart, but the other households proved that even fair math fails if the social dynamic is toxic. We need a rule that makes asking for the car feel like a transaction, not a favour.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, a transaction is only fair if the asset is ready. I found the car twice with the fuel light on and rubbish inside. That is not a social issue; it is a maintenance failure.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, maintenance is a separate line item. I am calculating the per-hour rate now. If the car is dirty, that is a service fee, not a fuel dispute.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shion, I agree. The short runs mean the car needs more care, which adds to the arranging time. I just want to know if that extra effort is worth it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, the arranging time is real, but it is secondary to the financial imbalance. We must quantify the subsidy before we optimize the workflow.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, quantifying the subsidy is necessary, but the other households showed that resentment comes from the *asking*, not the math. We need a booking system that removes the social debt entirely.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, a booking system is useless if the car is unusable. I found it twice with the fuel light on and rubbish inside. That is a maintenance failure, not a social one.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you are conflating hygiene with mechanics. I am calculating the per-hour rate. If the car is dirty, that is a service fee, not a fuel dispute.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Asuka, I understand the frustration. But the mechanic’s note about short runs explains the wear. We need to address the usage pattern, not just the mess.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I will propose a split: fixed costs divided equally, fuel paid by the driver. This removes the subsidy question entirely.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I support the split, but we must automate the booking. No more asking. The other households proved that the ""ask"" is where the relationship dies.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I support the split, but only if we mandate a handover checklist. Fuel light on and rubbish inside is a breach of contract, not a minor inconvenience.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,I support the split. The data proves the current guesswork is unsustainable. We need a strict per-hour rate to reflect the actual usage disparity.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I support the split. The diary shows the arranging time is the real cost. A clear system would help me stop feeling guilty about the hours.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
